        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.92,
          "end": 64.6,
          "en": "and in the index.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.6,
          "end": 66.82,
          "en": "So in the homepage component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.82,
          "end": 70.103,
          "en": "there I added the newsletter registration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.08,
          "end": 73.12,
          "en": "So if you install all dependencies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.12,
          "end": 75.93,
          "en": "and you run this updated snapshot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.93,
          "end": 80.12,
          "en": "then on the starting page, you will see that email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.12,
          "end": 82.52,
          "en": "this newsletter sign up part here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.52,
          "end": 84.763,
          "en": "And if you explore a single event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.4,
          "end": 88.19,
          "en": "there if you scroll to the bottom,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.19,
          "end": 90.37,
          "en": "you'll see the show comments button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.37,
          "end": 94.53999999999999,
          "en": "which you can click to view the comments forum",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.53999999999999,
          "end": 96.7,
          "en": "and some dummy comments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.7,
          "end": 99.43299999999999,
          "en": "which we're going to replace with actual comments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.43299999999999,
          "end": 101.523,
          "en": "throughout this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.39,
          "end": 104.62,
          "en": "Now that is the starting state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.62,
          "end": 106.95,
          "en": "And now I gotta challenge for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.95,
          "end": 110.71000000000001,
          "en": "I want you to add a couple of API routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.71000000000001,
          "end": 114.78999999999999,
          "en": "that handle the newsletter signup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.78999999999999,
          "end": 118.65,
          "en": "so that in the end handle an incoming email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.65,
          "end": 122.81,
          "en": "And then for the moment, maybe just log it to the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.81,
          "end": 126.65,
          "en": "so you don't need to add any code that writes to a file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.65,
          "end": 128.47,
          "en": "or talks to a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.47,
          "end": 132.46,
          "en": "though you can also do that as an extra exercise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.46,
          "end": 134.35,
          "en": "But for this task here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.35,
          "end": 137.27,
          "en": "just make sure that you accept some requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.27,
          "end": 139.61,
          "en": "from which you retrieve to email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.61,
          "end": 141.81,
          "en": "and make sure that such a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.81,
          "end": 144.73,
          "en": "is then sent from the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.73,
          "end": 147.46,
          "en": "From this newsletter registration component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.46,
          "end": 150.24,
          "en": "here in the registration handler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.24,
          "end": 152.31,
          "en": "Make sure you send the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.31,
          "end": 155.82,
          "en": "to that API route, which you should add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.82,
          "end": 159.15,
          "en": "You can also add validation for the user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 159.15,
          "end": 162.19,
          "en": "to check whether the entered email was valid,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.19,
          "end": 166.023,
          "en": "but that is up to you and not something you have to add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.9,
          "end": 170.93,
          "en": "Now, that is the first challenge, the first task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.93,
          "end": 172.72,
          "en": "it's not the only one though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.72,
          "end": 175.46,
          "en": "We also got to this comments section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.46,
          "end": 178.79,
          "en": "and there I want you to do a similar thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.79,
          "end": 183.79,
          "en": "Add another API route that allows users to submit comments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.65,
          "end": 189.48,
          "en": "and make sure that this API route is kind of dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.48,
          "end": 192.01,
          "en": "That the ID of the event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.01,
          "end": 194.28,
          "en": "to which the submitted common belongs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.28,
          "end": 196.79,
          "en": "is part of the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.79,
          "end": 198.67000000000002,
          "en": "of the API route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.67000000000002,
          "end": 202.51,
          "en": "So you'll need to create a dynamic API route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.51,
          "end": 205.52,
          "en": "Then again, handle incoming requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.52,
          "end": 208.93,
          "en": "and make sure you extract that submit a data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.93,
          "end": 211.74,
          "en": "and also handle the case data request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.74,
          "end": 213.64,
          "en": "is sent to fetch the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.64,
          "end": 218.38,
          "en": "So you will need to handle two different HTTP methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 218.38,
          "end": 222.21,
          "en": "For the newsletter API route, it was only one method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 222.21,
          "end": 224.84,
          "en": "you should handle post requests there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 224.84,
          "end": 226.82999999999998,
          "en": "But for the comments API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.82999999999998,
          "end": 230.34,
          "en": "you should handle two different HTTP methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.34,
          "end": 234.01,
          "en": "Incoming post requests which add a new comment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.01,
          "end": 237.393,
          "en": "and incoming GET requests, which fetch comments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.38,
          "end": 242.35,
          "en": "Again for the moment it is enough if you just log the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 242.35,
          "end": 245.33,
          "en": "if you just log something in your API route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245.33,
          "end": 248,
          "en": "You don't need to write any other logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 248,
          "end": 251.97,
          "en": "just return some dummy data in the GET request case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 251.97,
          "end": 256.41,
          "en": "and make sure you do send data and fetch data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.41,
          "end": 259.7,
          "en": "We have this add common handler in comments.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 259.7,
          "end": 264.38,
          "en": "where you should send that comments data to your API route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 264.38,
          "end": 268.37,
          "en": "And then also find a way of fetching comments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 268.37,
          "end": 272.78,
          "en": "when the list of comments here is shown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.78,
          "end": 274.47,
          "en": "So when that comment list is shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.47,
          "end": 278,
          "en": "make sure you then fetch comments from the API route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278,
          "end": 279.73,
          "en": "And again, for the moment it's okay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 279.73,
          "end": 282.29,
          "en": "if you just return some dummy data there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 282.29,
          "end": 285.57,
          "en": "just make sure you implement the base logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.57,
          "end": 288.67,
          "en": "and you add those API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.67,
          "end": 291.58,
          "en": "Now definitely try it on your own first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.58,
          "end": 293.78,
          "en": "In the next course lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 293.78,
          "end": 297.37,
          "en": "we're going to add those features together step-by-step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.37,
          "end": 300.98,
          "en": "and therefore of course also have a look at those lectures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 300.98,
          "end": 304.77,
          "en": "once you've tried it on your own to see how I solved it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 304.77,
          "end": 307.09,
          "en": "and to compare your solution to mine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 307.09,
          "end": 309.69,
          "en": "and maybe improve or fix your solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 309.69,
          "end": 311.7,
          "en": "if you got stuck somewhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 311.7,
          "end": 313.39300000000003,
          "en": "And with that, let's dive in.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
